<Layout title="Wealth Management for Business Owners | RIPL Wealth" description="Build your own finance company: put excess cash to work, grow wealth outside your business and make a future sale the cherry on top. RIPL Wealth planning."><section class="hero business-owner-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">BUSINESS OWNERS</div><h1><span class="business-title-line">You built the business</span> <span class="business-title-line">intentionally.</span><span class="business-hero-gold"><span class="business-title-line">Your personal wealth</span> <span class="business-title-line">deserves the same</span> <span class="business-title-line">treatment.</span></span></h1><p class="lead">Business owners are often excellent capital allocators inside the company. The personal side can be a different story.</p><a class="text-link business-question-jump" href="#finance-company">Explore Your Finance Company ↓</a></div></section><section class="section finance-company" id="finance-company"><div class="wrap"><div class="finance-company-intro-grid"><div class="finance-company-intro" data-reveal><div class="eyebrow">YOUR NEXT COMPANY DOESN’T NEED ANOTHER EMPLOYEE.</div><h2>Build a “finance company.”<br/><span class="business-hero-gold">Put your excess cash to work.</span></h2><p class="lead">You know how to build a business that makes money. Now let’s give some of that money a job outside the business.</p><p>Think of it as your own finance company: a dedicated investment strategy funded with capital you can put to work after your operating needs, reserves and tax obligations are accounted for. We help you organize it, invest it with purpose and keep it connected to the life you want to build.</p></div><FinanceCompanyFlow/></div><div class="finance-company-benefits" data-reveal><article><span aria-hidden="true">0</span><h3>Employees to hire.</h3><p>No recruiting, staffing or payroll to manage.</p></article><article><span aria-hidden="true">0</span><h3>Operating business to run.</h3><p>No new location, inventory or customer pipeline to build.</p></article><article><span aria-hidden="true">1</span><h3>Clear job for your capital.</h3><p>Build wealth outside the company you already work hard to run.</p></article></div><p class="small finance-company-note">“Finance company” describes our planning approach, rather than a required new legal entity. There is no additional operating business overhead; investment and advisory costs still apply.</p><div class="finance-company-sale"><div><div class="eyebrow">BUILD WEALTH ALONG THE WAY.</div><h3>Selling your business should be<br/><span class="business-hero-gold">the cherry on top.</span><span class="finance-company-mountain">Not the top of the mountain.</span></h3></div><div><p>What if a future sale added to the financial life you’ve already built, instead of being the event you’re counting on to make it all work?</p><p>That’s the goal. Keep building a strong business while deliberately growing wealth outside it. A sale can then create more options, rather than carry the whole plan.</p><p>We start by identifying what is genuinely available to invest, where it belongs and when you may need it. Your CPA helps confirm the tax and ownership implications before money moves. Your investment plan reflects your goals, time horizon and willingness to take risk.</p><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Let’s Build Your Finance Company</a><p class="small">Investments can lose value. Growth and a future business sale are not guaranteed.</p></div></div><div class="related"><a href="/business-owners/excess-business-cash/">What should I do with excess business cash?</a> · <a href="/business-owners/build-wealth-outside-business/">How do I build wealth outside my business?</a></div></div></section><section class="section dark business-closing"><div class="wrap business-closing-grid"><figure class="business-closing-portrait"><div class="business-closing-photo"><img src="/images/adam-video-shoot.jpg" alt="Adam Kasick in conversation during a video shoot" width="1280" height="1920" loading="lazy"/></div></figure><div class="business-closing-copy"><blockquote class="business-owner-quote"><p>“Your business may be your greatest asset. It doesn’t have to be your entire financial plan.”</p><cite>Adam Kasick · Wealth Manager</cite></blockquote><p class="lead">Your business has a plan for its capital. Your personal wealth should too.</p><p>Let’s look at what you’ve built, what your business actually needs, and what you want your wealth to make possible.</p><div class="business-closing-actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Start the Conversation</a><a class="text-link" href="/business-owners/10-money-questions/">Explore Business Owner Questions</a></div></div></div></section><section class="section business-question-cards" id="business-owner-questions"><div class="wrap"><div class="grid"><a class="card" href="/business-owners/excess-business-cash/"><h3>What should I do with excess business cash?</h3><p>Decide what the cash needs to do before deciding where it belongs.</p><span class="card-question-link">Explore this question →</span></a><a class="card" href="/business-owners/how-much-cash/"><h3>How much cash should I keep in my business?</h3><p>Operating needs, protection and opportunity before arbitrary percentages.</p><span class="card-question-link">Explore this question →</span></a><a class="card" href="/business-owners/build-wealth-outside-business/"><h3>How do I build wealth outside my business?</h3><p>Build a personal balance sheet without blindly starving a successful company.</p><span class="card-question-link">Explore this question →</span></a><a class="card" href="/business-owners/business-to-personal-wealth/"><h3>How do I turn business wealth into personal wealth?</h3><p>Give capital jobs on both sides of your financial life.</p><span class="card-question-link">Explore this question →</span></a><a class="card" href="/business-owners/net-worth-in-business/"><h3>How much of my net worth should be tied to my business?</h3><p>Understand concentration without letting a pie chart make the decision.</p><span class="card-question-link">Explore this question →</span></a><a class="card" href="/business-owners/before-selling-business/"><h3>What should I do before selling my business?</h3><p>Plan for the wealth before the wire arrives.</p><span class="card-question-link">Explore this question →</span></a><a class="card" href="/business-owners/after-selling-business/"><h3>What should I do after selling my business?</h3><p>Turn sale proceeds into a personal capital allocation strategy.</p><span class="card-question-link">Explore this question →</span></a><a class="card" href="/business-owners/qsbs/"><h3>What is QSBS?</h3><p>A potentially valuable tax opportunity worth understanding before you sell.</p><span class="card-question-link">Explore this question →</span></a></div></div></section><BusinessOwnerCheckupCTA eyebrow="YOU KNOW YOUR BUSINESS. HOW WELL DO YOU KNOW YOUR MONEY?" heading="You built a successful business." highlight="What’s driving your money decisions?" body="Your approach to money has helped you get here. Discover your wealth persona, the strengths you bring, and the patterns worth a second look." button="Take the Quiz →" note="About 3 minutes. Insights based on your answers."/><TaxQuestion context="business"/>
</Layout>